      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">AI Sticker Generator</p>

      <h1>AI Sticker Generator</h1>

      <p>
        Generate custom stickers from a text prompt or portrait. The AI sticker generator is free to
        try with no sign up: guests get 3 generations, then can download PNG or WebP files.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#generator">Generate a Free Sticker</a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Free, no sign up</h2>

        <p>
          Start generating without creating an account or adding a payment card. The guest trial
          covers 3 sticker generations so you can test the tool first.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Text or portrait</h2>

        <p>
          Write a short prompt for mascots, reactions, and characters, or upload a clear portrait
          for an avatar-style sticker.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Download-ready files</h2>

        <p>
          Completed stickers can be saved as PNG for editing or WebP for smaller web and chat
          assets. Failed generations return the credit automatically.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to use the AI sticker generator</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>Open the generator. No sign up is required for the 3 free guest generations.</li>

        <li>Write a short prompt or upload a portrait, then generate the sticker.</li>

        <li>Each generation uses 1 credit. Failed generations return the credit automatically.</li>

        <li>Download completed stickers as PNG or WebP from history.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>AI sticker generator prompt examples</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>cute fox mascot sticker, happy face, clean white border, simple background</code>
        <code>sleepy cat holding a coffee cup, kawaii sticker, rounded outline</code>
        <code>portrait avatar sticker, expressive face, crisp border, profile ready</code>
        <code>surprised frog reaction sticker, bold expression, chat sticker style</code>
        <code>friendly robot waving, bright colors, thick outline, simple sticker background</code>
        <code>cozy mushroom character, tiny umbrella, soft colors, rounded sticker silhouette</code>
        <code>happy bakery mascot, smiling croissant, clean border, warm pastel palette</code>
        <code>sleepy moon and stars sticker, calm face, dark blue outline, simple shape</code>
        <code>proud garden snail mascot, expressive eyes, leafy accent, crisp white border</code>
        <code>excited game controller character, joyful expression, bold chat reaction sticker</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to write a better AI sticker prompt</h2>

      <p>
        Start with one subject. Then add the emotion, pose, style, border, and background direction
        that matter most. For example, a sleepy cat holding a coffee cup gives the generator a clear
        subject and action; a kawaii sticker with a rounded outline and simple background adds a consistent
        visual direction without filling the prompt with competing details.
      </p>

      <p>
        Short prompts are easier to improve. If the subject is correct but the expression is wrong,
        change the emotion. If the silhouette is cluttered, remove scene details and ask for a simple
        background. If you are making a set, repeat the same border, palette, and style language so
        the stickers feel related.
      </p>

      <p>
        Text prompts work well for mascots, objects, food, animals, fictional characters, and chat
        reactions. Portrait mode is better when the source image itself is important. Use a clear
        photo with one main subject, then add only the style instructions needed to guide the final
        sticker.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Choosing a download format</h2>

      <p>
        Download PNG when you need broad editing compatibility or want to continue working in a
        design tool. Download WebP when file size matters for a website, preview, or messaging
        workflow. The app provides finished image files. Chat platforms apply their own rules for
        dimensions, transparency, animation, and pack setup; the numbers are listed on the Photo to
        Sticker platform requirements page.
      </p>

      <p>
        Guests can access generated results through the current guest identity. Signing in attaches
        eligible guest-generated stickers to an account for continued account access, and one-time
        credit packs are available when the free trial is used.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Free AI sticker generator with no sign up</h2>

      <p>
        The guest trial covers the whole flow: 3 generations, 1 credit each, and a failed generation
        returns its credit automatically. No account or payment card is needed to generate or
        download a sticker from history as PNG or WebP.
      </p>

      <p>
        Stickers are generated at 1024 x 1024 px, while chat platforms ask for smaller artwork in
        their own formats, so plan on one resize pass after downloading. The generator produces the
        image file; building a pack is a separate destination-platform step. See
        <.link navigate={~p"/photo-to-sticker"}>platform requirements for WhatsApp, Telegram and Discord</.link>.
      </p>

      <p>
        After the trial, an account is only needed for more credits, saved history, and one-time
        credit packs. There is no subscription.
      </p>

      <h2>Related tools</h2>
      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/"}>AI Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sticker-maker-online"}>Sticker Maker Online</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/custom-sticker-maker"}>Custom Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/christmas-ai-sticker-maker"}>Christmas AI Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/photo-to-sticker"}>Photo to Sticker</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2>AI sticker generator FAQ</h2>
    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is this AI sticker generator free?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Guests can create up to 3 stickers for free with no sign up and no payment card.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do I need an account to generate stickers?</summary>

        <p>
          No. Guests can create up to 3 stickers without an account and access generated results
          through the current guest identity. Sign in to buy credits and attach eligible results to
          your account later.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What can I generate?</summary>

        <p>
          You can generate prompt-based stickers, portrait stickers, avatars, mascots, and small
          batches.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I write a good sticker prompt?</summary>

        <p>
          Start with one subject, then add an emotion, pose, style, border, and simple background.
          Short prompts are easier to refine than crowded scene descriptions.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I generate a sticker from a portrait?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Switch to portrait mode and upload a clear JPG or PNG with one visible face, good
          lighting, and minimal blur.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What is the difference between PNG and WebP?</summary>

        <p>
          PNG is convenient for editing and compatibility. WebP is usually smaller for websites,
          previews, and chat workflows.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do failed generations use a credit?</summary>

        <p>
          A failed generation automatically returns its credit. You can retry with a shorter prompt
          or a clearer portrait.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
